Experiment with subsurface scattering shaders and high-resolution textures for foliage and wildlife. Utilize displacement maps to add subtle surface details like bark bumps and feather imperfections. Employ particle effects to simulate realistic rain, mist, or falling leaves.  Consider using a variety of models and textures – think of the diverse range of plant species and animal types you’d find in a real jungle. Don't be afraid to experiment with subtle variations in color and texture to add depth and realism. Finally, use a high-quality rendering engine to achieve a polished, immersive final product.

